===Alternative forms===
* {{l|nl|veugel}} (obsolete)
* {{l|nl|fogel}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|vōgel}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|fogal}}, {{m|odt|vogal}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*fugl}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*fuglaz}}.

Cognate with {{cog|de|Vogel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈvoːɣəl/|qual2=Hollandic|[ˈfoʊ̯χɔɫ]}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-vogel.ogg|audio}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|vo|gel}}
* {{rhyme|nl|oːɣəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|m|-s|pl2=-@en|vogeltje|dim2=vogelijn}}

# {{topics|nl|Vertebrates}} [[bird]], any member of the class [[Aves]]
# a [[feathered]] target in [[archery]] or [[shooting]]
#: {{syn|nl|gaai}}
# {{lb|nl|figuratively||slang}} A [[dude]], a {{l|en|cat}} {{gloss|slang term for a man}}.

====Usage notes====
The word ''vogel'' is one of the few words where the obsolete Dutch diminutive suffix {{m|nl|-lijn}} can still be encountered: {{m|nl|vogelijn||little bird}} is chiefly poetic and can be found in poems and songs, but is not often used elsewhere.

